1788559068.911 14:57:48 RECV method=tools/call id=3 params={"name": "ask_user", "arguments": {"questions": [{"question": "Question 2 \u2014 where the data lives (the part of Q1 still open).\n\nOn the server side: what's the backend today \u2014 your own API over Postgres/MySQL, a BaaS (Firebase/Supabase/Amplify), or something else? And does the API expose per-note CRUD, or bulk/batch endpoints too?\n\nOn the device side: is there any persistence in the RN app today \u2014 AsyncStorage, MMKV, SQLite (op-sqlite/expo-sqlite/WatermelonDB), Realm \u2014 or is it fetch-on-mount into Redux/Zustand/React Query with nothing durable?\n\n(Also useful: bare RN or Expo? That constrains which storage/sync libraries are even available to you.)", "options": ["Own REST API over Postgres, per-note CRUD only, AsyncStorage for auth token but no note persistence", "Own API over Postgres, has batch/delta endpoints, SQLite on device already", "Firebase/Supabase \u2014 the SDK is effectively the backend", "Something else \u2014 I'll describe it"]}]}, "_meta": {"claudecode/toolUseId": "toolu_01QnzshbNHRGdY2WvCjoCzao", "progressToken": 3}}
1788559068.911 14:57:48 TOOLCALL BLOCKING START
1788559072.381 14:57:52 TOOLCALL UNBLOCKED answer="Conflicts are rare but must never lose data - I'd rather keep both versions than overwrite."
1788559088.494 14:58:08 RECV method=tools/call id=4 params={"name": "ask_user", "arguments": {"questions": [{"question": "Question 3 \u2014 what \"keep both\" should actually mean to the user.\n\nWhen the same note was edited on two devices while one was offline, which of these is the behavior you want?\n\n- **Fork the note**: the note splits into two visible notes (\"Grocery list\" and \"Grocery list (conflicted copy from iPhone, Mar 3)\"), user reconciles by hand. Simple, honest, never loses a byte \u2014 but clutters the list.\n- **Merge automatically, keep both edits**: character-level merge (CRDT) so both devices' typing lands in one note and nobody sees a conflict at all. Best UX, most machinery, and can produce interleaved nonsense if both edited the same sentence.\n- **Auto-merge when the edits don't overlap, fork when they do**: middle ground, more moving parts.\n- **Keep one, but preserve the loser as version history**: the list stays clean, the other version is recoverable from a \"history\" screen rather than sitting in the note list.\n\nAlso: does concurrent editing of the *same* note on two devices actually happen for your users (shared accounts, phone + tablet), or is \"conflict\" mostly the rare case of one person's second device having stale state?", "options": ["Fork into a visibly conflicted copy", "Auto-merge everything with a CRDT", "Auto-merge non-overlapping, fork on true overlap", "Keep one, loser goes to version history"]}]}, "_meta": {"claudecode/toolUseId": "toolu_013LFadbTWH7ZvgQtU5HNwZY", "progressToken": 4}}
